12111	{"artifactId":"LLD-99a7f5dc933a8456-s1","entry":{"id":"review-37779e397166131e5a347fc07d040785","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T05:33:51.059Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"AC1 ('Active but slow reviews are not killed merely because a size-based expected duration elapsed') is designed: the task no longer has a fixed wall-clock cutoff.","evidence":"LLD §2.1 postcondition states 'No fixed task wall-clock cutoff' and §7 migration step 2 removes the old size deadlines for task mode only; matches the upstream acceptance criterion verbatim.","action":"Confirmed against plans/progress-based-review-timeouts.future-work.json AC list and the LLD's own postconditions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"AC2 ('Remote silence, ongoing tool execution, local contention, tool hangs and genuine inactivity have distinguishable diagnostics and tested intervention behavior') is fully designed.","evidence":"§5 Error paths lumps 'Model/network silence' and 'local contention' into a single error case with one detection mechanism (monotonic meaningful-activity age) and one diagnostic; the design never distinguishes remote-silence from local-contention, nor gives either a separate diagnostic from genuine task-inactivity. The test-strategy acceptance row for ac2 ('30-minute quiet grace; heartbeat does not renew; tool age separate') does not test for distinguishability either. [files: docs/standalone/preserve-useful-review-work-permissive-progress-E2026110199a7f5dc/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Ask the author to add a distinct diagnostic/detection path for local machine contention vs remote model/network silence, or to narrow AC2's wording and get it reconfirmed with the user, since the design currently treats them as one case.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today's task review applies size-based 5/10/15-minute (S/M/L) host cancellation, as the design's 'current behaviour'/migration section states.","evidence":"coordinator.ts:99 `allowance = { S: 300000, M: 600000, L: 900000 }[task.size]` races a setTimeout against the provider call; controller.ts:96 `remaining(){... {S:300000,M:600000,L:900000}[task.size]-...}` and exposes `remainingMs` in every ControllerFrame (controller.ts:131). [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/controller.ts]","action":"Read both files' task-loop and timer logic directly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"'Claude and Codex native event adapters normalize only observable metadata' (§2.2 precondition) presumes a live, in-flight event stream already exists for both CLIs that a new adapter only needs to normalize.","evidence":"Every claude invocation in cli-provider.ts (complete:236, completeStructured:350, runEditSession:419, reviewSessionOnce/claudeReviewSessionArgs:494+104-113) uses `--print --output-format json`, which returns ONE JSON envelope only after the whole call finishes — there is no partial/stream output mode in use, so no 'model_output'/'tool_started' signal is observable mid-run for Claude today. For codex, runCodex (cli-provider.ts:597-629) also only parses the JSONL events AFTER the subprocess exits (`out.stdout.split('\\n')`); the only thing read incrementally today is the raw stdout buffer for the stall-watchdog regex (process-group.ts child.stdout 'data' handler), not structured events. Building the new monitor on an assumed-already-observable event stream, with no corresponding change to the CLI invocation flags, would leave Claude sessions with effectively no mid-run activity signal at all. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/shared/process-group.ts]","action":"Add a concrete contract item for switching the claude invocation(s) used by runReviewSession to a streaming/partial output mode (or an equivalent mechanism) and for incrementally parsing codex's JSONL as it arrives, not only after exit; without this the activity-based design cannot actually detect 'meaningful activity' mid-session for either CLI as currently wired, especially claude.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"`ReviewActivityMonitor` and `ReviewActivityEvent`/`ReviewActivitySnapshot` are genuinely new — they do not already exist in the codebase under another name.","evidence":"Searched src/ for ReviewActivityMonitor / ReviewActivityEvent / ReviewActivitySnapshot: the only hits are the LLD artifact itself, the generated LLD.md, and .insrc review-run transcripts of this very review — no pre-existing implementation.","action":"grep across the repo for the three new type/class names.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"'Existing command-specific tool termination' / 'existing tool limits' that §2.1's postcondition and §5's error case say remain independent of the new monitor are an already-existing mechanism in this codebase that can simply be kept.","evidence":"codeTaskCommands() (policy.ts) only computes which Bash commands a reviewer session is ALLOWED to run (`--allowedTools Bash(<command>)`); it does not impose any per-command or per-tool-call time limit. A repo-wide search for a tool-call timeout mechanism inside the task-review/reviewer-session path turned up nothing — the only 'tool timeout' hits found are unrelated daemon tool-exec/git/gh timeouts, not anything bounding an individual Bash call a claude/codex reviewer session makes internally. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/policy.ts]","action":"Ask the author to name the specific existing mechanism (or CLI-internal behavior) they mean by 'existing command-specific tool termination', since none was found in this repo; if it is actually the CLI binary's own opaque internal tool timeout, say so explicitly rather than implying this codebase already enforces it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"§3.2's call sites for removing the size-based allowance (coordinator.ts, controller.ts, daemon/task-review-rpc.ts) name every file that actually holds the {S,M,L} timing logic to be removed.","evidence":"The allowance map and timer/race logic live exactly in coordinator.ts (lines 99-147) and controller.ts (lines 96-150, 137-150); task-review-rpc.ts has no timing logic of its own (only request validation/dispatch to the coordinator), so listing it is harmless even though it carries nothing to change directly. [files: src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts]","action":"Read task-review-rpc.ts in full; confirmed no deadline/allowance code lives there.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"§3.1's call sites for the new `ReviewActivityEvent` (types.ts, cli-provider.ts, process-group.ts) are the complete set of sites that need to change.","evidence":"Per §2.1, 'each task execution owns one monitor', so coordinator.ts and controller.ts — the two places that actually run a task and would construct/feed a per-task ReviewActivityMonitor from the new event-callback in ReviewSessionOpts — are not listed as call sites for the event type, even though they are the consumers that must wire the callback through to the monitor and act on its `incomplete`/cancel outcome. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/controller.ts]","action":"Add coordinator.ts and controller.ts to §3.1's call-site list (or make explicit in §2.1/§3.2 that the monitor construction and event wiring happen there), so the task-execution integration point is not missed during build.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"'No rewrite of submitted packets, checkpoint history or CR schema' (§7 Backward compat) holds — the checkpoint's on-disk shape is untouched by this design.","evidence":"ReviewCheckpoint keeps `schemaVersion: 1` and ReviewAttempt's header fields (activeTaskId, interrupted, selectedTaskIds, etc., contracts.ts:74-79) are exactly what the design's postconditions reuse (e.g. 'delete entry.header.activeTaskId' pattern); the design's new tool-activity tracking is described as ephemeral/in-memory (§3.1 'Ephemeral typed events'), so nothing new is added to the persisted checkpoint shape. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts]","action":"Read the ReviewAttempt/ReviewCheckpoint interfaces and cross-checked against the design's stated migration steps.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'Tool hangs or CLI never exits after valid feedback' error case is actually detectable as designed ('Separate active tool age plus existing tool limits').","evidence":"Detection for this case depends on the same 'existing tool limits' this review could not find a concrete implementation for (see new-versus-reuse finding on policy.ts/codeTaskCommands). Without a located existing per-tool bound, the claim that 'existing tool limit or review inactivity intervenes, no unbounded lease' (edge-case table) rests only on the NEW 30-minute session-level monitor, not on any separate existing tool-level limit, which weakens — but does not by itself invalidate — the detectability claim. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/policy.ts]","action":"Same as the new-versus-reuse finding: have the author name the concrete existing mechanism, or drop the reference to an 'existing tool limit' and rely solely on the new monitor plus any new tool-record aging the author intends to add.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every upstream acceptance criterion maps to a named test, including AC2's 'distinguishable diagnostics' requirement across remote-silence, tool-execution, local-contention, tool-hang and genuine-inactivity.","evidence":"The acceptance-mapping table's ac2 row only states '30-minute quiet grace; heartbeat does not renew; tool age separate' — it tests the grace timing and heartbeat-rejection, not that remote-silence is diagnostically distinguishable from local-contention as AC2 requires (both are one undifferentiated error case in §5, consistent with the coverage-of-intent finding above). [files: docs/standalone/preserve-useful-review-work-permissive-progress-E2026110199a7f5dc/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Once the coverage-of-intent gap on distinguishable diagnostics is resolved, add/adjust the ac2 test row (and its integration-test fixtures) to actually assert the distinction, rather than only the aggregate grace/heartbeat behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":3,"low":7,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-11-01T05:33:51.059Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
