579	{"artifactId":"LLD-99a7f5dc933a8456-s1","entry":{"id":"b1c0ce59d9374df49777c0d3d278b155","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T06:04:04.421Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":2,"contentHash":"11e42fa94379fcf979481f71ff0fbfea64f57bc5c459a43aaae70ac599ff78fd"},"outcome":{"result":"author-correction","summary":"Fix HIGH/MED: specify native stream work, factual contention/wait diagnostics, complete coordinator/controller call sites and AC2 tests; remove unsupported existing per-tool-limit claims."},"addresses":"all"}}
13060	{"artifactId":"LLD-99a7f5dc933a8456-s1","entry":{"id":"review-d454349e45437794ad8c82856c045ae8","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T06:04:18.175Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The four acceptance criteria (ac1-ac4) in the test-strategy table map to the design's own decisions: no fixed task cutoff (a2 chosen), 30-minute inactivity grace with non-renewing heartbeats/polls, diagnostic classification facts, and daemon/controller parity with no retry.","evidence":"Section 6 'Acceptance mapping' ties ac1-ac4 to concrete test subjects that match sections 2.1/2.2/3.4/8.2 of the same document; no decision or non-goal in the body is left unmapped.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"'S4 owns presentation' / 'S4 consumes normalized activity for presentation' refers to a real, tracked sibling Story that the diagnostic snapshot (section 3.4) is designed to serve.","evidence":"The artifact's own meta confirms `standalone: true, sizeClass: 'feature'` (LLD-99a7f5dc933a8456-s1.json) with 'Standalone feature — no parent HLD'. A standalone design.story has no sibling stories (s2/s3/s4): only `docs/standalone/preserve-useful-review-work-permissive-progress-E2026110199a7f5dc/S001/LLD.md` exists for this epic hash, and no S4 artifact of any kind exists anywhere in the repo. The design repeatedly defers the snapshot's consumer to an 'S4' that is not a tracked entity, so that deferred scope (how/whether the diagnostic facts are ever surfaced) has no actual destination on the ledger. [files: docs/standalone/preserve-useful-review-work-permissive-progress-E2026110199a7f5dc/S001/LLD.md, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-99a7f5dc933a8456-s1.json]","action":"Either drop the 'S4' framing and state the snapshot is unconsumed/internal-only for this Story, or file the presentation work as a real follow-on Story before relying on 'S4' as a design boundary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Daemon-side task review currently cancels a task on a fixed size-based allowance of 5/10/15 minutes (S/M/L), exactly as section 3.2 claims is being removed.","evidence":"coordinator.ts:99 `const started = now(), allowance = { S: 300000, M: 600000, L: 900000 }[task.size];` followed by a `Promise.race` against an `expired` timer at that allowance — this is live code, not yet changed. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The controller-driven path independently recomputes the same size-based allowance and exposes `remainingMs` to the caller, matching the design's claim that 'controller remainingMs semantics' exist today and are being removed.","evidence":"controller.ts:96 `private remaining():number{const task=this.current();return task&&this.started!==undefined?{S:300000,M:600000,L:900000}[task.size]-(this.clock()-this.started):0;}` and `ControllerFrame.remainingMs` (controller.ts:25) returned from `frame()`. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/controller.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"`ReviewActivityEvent`, `ReviewActivityMonitor`, `ReviewActivitySnapshot` and `ReviewInactivityError` are genuinely new — no prior implementation exists to confuse with 'reuse'.","evidence":"A repo-wide grep for these four identifiers returned zero matches outside this LLD.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design correctly reuses existing cancellation/cleanup machinery (AbortController/AbortSignal wiring, `ReviewSessionTimeoutError`, process-group SIGKILL cleanup) rather than inventing new ones.","evidence":"cli-provider.ts:90 defines `ReviewSessionTimeoutError`; `ReviewSessionOpts.signal` (shared/types.ts:264) and `runInProcessGroup`'s `onAbort`/`kill()` (process-group.ts:106-118) already implement exactly the cancel-and-cleanup path the design says it keeps ('Process group cleanup retained'). [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/shared/process-group.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The 'NEW REQUIRED PROVIDER WORK' call-site inventory (section 2.2/3.1, listing only cli-provider.ts) is the complete set of `runReviewSession` implementors whose contract is changing.","evidence":"`OllamaProvider` also implements `LLMProvider.runReviewSession` (exercised by src/agent/providers/__tests__/ollama-review-session.test.ts) and is a reachable provider for the 'review' role: role-taxonomy.ts marks 'review' critical/defaultTier 'core', and config/analyze.ts's `TierModel.runner` is explicitly 'closed to the k1 CLI/Ollama set' — i.e. a repo can configure the core tier's runner to Ollama. The design's new opt-in `ReviewSessionOpts` fields (activity callbacks, task mode) would reach Ollama's implementation too, but no Ollama-side handling, fallback, or explicit non-support is specified anywhere in the LLD. [files: src/agent/providers/ollama-review-session.ts, src/config/role-taxonomy.ts, src/config/analyze.ts]","action":"Name OllamaProvider explicitly: either extend it to honor/ignore the new opts safely, or add an explicit precondition that activity-supervised task mode requires a CLI (claude/codex) provider and document the refusal/fallback when 'review' resolves to Ollama.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Removing `ControllerFrame.remainingMs` is safe because no caller outside controller.ts/its own tests reads that field.","evidence":"Grep for `remainingMs` across src/ shows all `ControllerFrame`-side usages confined to controller.ts and controller.test.ts; src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/controller.ts (a consumer of ControllerFrame-shaped flows elsewhere) has no `remainingMs` reference. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/controller.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new activity/tool-tracking state can be kept out of the persisted checkpoint without a schema migration, as the design implies ('Document additive wire capability ... without changing checkpoints').","evidence":"`CheckpointSchema` in contracts.ts is declared with `{additionalProperties:false}` at every object level (header, review-response, checkpoint), so any new persisted field would be a breaking schema change; the design keeps `ReviewActivityEvent`/monitor state and the diagnostic snapshot explicitly 'ephemeral' and 'bounded, emits only at inactivity' rather than durable checkpoint fields, avoiding that migration. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The task-based code-review publication record (`TaskBasedCodeReviewRecord`, schemaVersion 2) is unaffected by the timing-policy change, consistent with 'No rewrite of submitted packets, checkpoint history or CR schema.'","evidence":"contracts.ts:85-88 defines `TaskBasedCodeReviewRecord` purely from `CompletedReviewSummary`/`TaskReviewResult`, neither of which the design proposes changing (only `header`/timer semantics inside `ReviewAttempt` and the ephemeral activity layer change). [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"This LLD does not redesign anything owned by another Story or Epic shared contract, consistent with its own 'Standalone feature — no parent HLD' framing.","evidence":"The artifact's meta confirms `standalone:true`, `hldAmendmentsApplied: []`, `adjacentBoundaries: []`, and no HLD exists for epicHash 99a7f5dc933a8456 — there is no other Story/shared contract in scope for this change to encroach on; the only loose end is the undefined-but-referenced 'S4' already flagged under coverage-of-intent, which is a forward-reference problem, not an actual boundary violation. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-99a7f5dc933a8456-s1.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The local-contention diagnostic (event-loop delay via `node:perf_hooks.monitorEventLoopDelay`, OS load via `node:os.loadavg`/`availableParallelism`) is backed by APIs that actually exist on the project's Node 20+/22 runtime.","evidence":"Both `perf_hooks.monitorEventLoopDelay` and `os.loadavg`/`os.availableParallelism` are standard Node.js APIs available well before Node 20 (availableParallelism landed in Node 18.4/19.4), matching CLAUDE.md's stated Node 20+ runtime, so the detection described in section 3.4/Error paths is technically buildable as described.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's heaviest new-capability risk (incremental native event parsing distinguishing tool-run/timeout from plain silence) is honestly flagged as unverified rather than asserted as working.","evidence":"Section 2.2 explicitly states 'Verify installed CLI flags and event fixtures before wiring; capability failure is explicit, never fake progress,' and the current `runCodex` implementation (cli-provider.ts:605-611) already tolerantly skips unparseable JSONL lines rather than assuming a fixed event shape — the design's caution is consistent with how fragile the existing event parsing already is. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The claimed 'fake clocks and fake CLI processes' test infrastructure already exists and is exercised for the timing paths this design changes, supporting the test-strategy's unit/integration levels.","evidence":"coordinator.ts/controller.ts both accept an injectable `timer`/`now` (`deps.timer`, `this.deps.now`), and controller.test.ts (e.g. line 94/98) and coordinator.test.ts already drive deterministic fake clocks against the exact size-based timers this design replaces. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/controller.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/coordinator.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The test strategy's 'contract' level ('unchanged non-task bounded provider calls') covers the OllamaProvider implementation of `runReviewSession` the same way it covers CliProvider.","evidence":"The test-strategy's integration/contract fixtures (section 6) name only Claude stream-json and Codex JSONL fixtures; OllamaProvider has its own `runReviewSession` test suite (ollama-review-session.test.ts) exercising the same `ReviewSessionOpts` surface, but no test subject or fixture addresses whether Ollama's existing non-task reviewer-session behavior stays bounded/unchanged once the opt-in task-mode fields are added to the shared opts type — the same gap identified under change-sites. [files: src/agent/providers/__tests__/ollama-review-session.test.ts]","action":"Add an explicit 'contract' test subject asserting OllamaProvider's runReviewSession ignores/rejects the new activity-mode opts without behavior change, mirroring the CliProvider coverage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":3,"low":12,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-11-01T06:04:18.175Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
